{
  "name": "Forest rave",
  "notes": "Witch's first music style (2026-10-04), from the genres in Ed's reference playlist (a screenshot of its track list he shared in the music builder's session that day: melodic organic house and melodic techno, dark synth and French electro, chiptune and bubblegum electro, hyperpop, dark minimal pop and phonk). Nothing is taken from any track: every sound is synthesised and every tune generated. it starts as warm melodic, organic house in the dark forest (marimba plucks, soft pads, shakers), deepens into melodic techno with strings, turns to dark synth-electro (driving saw bass, gated pads, supersaw leads), sparkles into chiptune and bubblegum electro (square arps, bouncing octave bass), and ends in phonk (a sliding 808, a cowbell hook, trap hats) for the frantic finale. Breakdowns go minimal and dark (finger snaps over a sub). Sections are named in the arc below, one step per wave; the last step repeats.",
